<article class="prose">
    <h1>Pay people right, and on time</h1>
    <p class="prose-sub">Why we built WageHarbor.</p>

    <blockquote>“Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.”<br /><small class="text-muted" style="font-family:inherit;font-size:.9rem">Prophet Muhammad ﷺ · Sunan Ibn Majah 2443</small></blockquote>

    <p>Fourteen centuries ago, that teaching made a simple point that every business owner still feels today: when someone has done the work, they have earned their pay, and holding it back is a wrong. Payday isn't paperwork. It's rent, groceries and peace of mind for the people who keep a business running.</p>

    <p>Yet for many small businesses, payroll is the hardest part of having a team. Software is expensive, tax rules change every year, and employees wait on HR just to see a pay stub. Mistakes and delays land on the people who can least afford them.</p>

    <h2>What WageHarbor does</h2>
    <p>WageHarbor gives a small business the tools a large one takes for granted:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Correct pay:</strong> federal, Social Security, Medicare, state and unemployment taxes are calculated for every paycheck, with overtime and time off built in.</li>
        <li><strong>On-time pay:</strong> a clear calculate → approve → pay flow, with a direct-deposit file ready for your bank.</li>
        <li><strong>Open pay:</strong> every employee can see, print and save their own pay stubs and balances, any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Private pay:</strong> each company's data is kept apart, and sensitive numbers are encrypted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Fairness is practical.</strong> Paying correctly and promptly is the most concrete way a business shows respect for its people.</li>
        <li><strong>Small businesses deserve good tools.</strong> That's why WageHarbor costs about a quarter of similar apps, and nothing if you have one person on payroll. We're here to serve, not to squeeze: there are no ads, we never sell your data, and we charge only what it takes to run the service well.</li>
        <li><strong>Trust is earned with honesty.</strong> We tell you what WageHarbor does and doesn't do. For example, it calculates payroll taxes but you file them, and we'll keep it that clear.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="prose-cta">
        <p>Ready to run your first payroll?</p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
            <a href="Account/Register" class="btn btn-primary">Register your company</a>
            <a href="help/company" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Read the company guide</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
